1
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:13,900
A full week. Every tile on it belongs to someone.

2
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:21,800
Thursday, three o’clock.

3
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:25,400
The sales director needs figures for a tender by Friday noon.

4
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,400
Friday belongs to the harbour costing.

5
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,300
Both answers sound helpful.

6
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:40,200
In both, the project manager finds out after his costing has moved.

7
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,500
Something was going to move anyway.

8
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:50,300
The question is who hears in time to say no.

9
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:57,200
I can have the figures by Friday noon if the harbour costing moves to Monday.

10
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:00,700
I’ll check that with its project manager and tell you by four.

11
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:05,600
He says no. Good.

12
00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:08,000
That is what the question was for.

13
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:15,900
Now it is a real clash, and no rule says who wins.

14
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,200
That is your manager’s call.

15
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:24,300
Send Nadia a puzzle and she answers both.

16
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:30,100
Send her a plan, and she can approve it in one word.
